Genuine failure found and fixed during testing
Case 5 (simulated service unavailable) initially failed for the wrong reason: the mock “service down” area code did not match the area_code format check, so it was rejected as a validation_error before the code ever reached the outage-status lookup that was supposed to raise “unavailable.” This masked the failure path we actually needed to test. The fix was to give the simulated-down area a code in the correct format (DWN-99) so it passes validation and correctly reaches the unavailable branch. This is left in as documented evidence rather than silently corrected, since it demonstrates a real class of bug: validation order can accidentally hide the failure case you meant to test.
Human-approval flow, verified
After Case 6 creates a ticket (status: pending_approval), calling approve_ticket (ticket_id, approved_by="human_agent_dennise") is the only way its status becomes created. No code path inside create_support_ticket itself can set status to created — the approval step is a structurally separate function, not a flag the AI or the customer can set.
